/.idea
/.vscode
/.fleet
/.nova
/.phpunit.cache
/node_modules
/public/build
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
.DS_Store
# Every environment file except the committed template. Written as "ignore all, then unignore
# the example" rather than as a list of known suffixes: the list approach missed `.env.testing`
# and `.env.local`, and the failure mode of a missed suffix is a committed credential.
.env*
!.env.example
.phpactor.json
.phpunit.result.cache
auth.json
docker-compose.override.yml
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
/coverage
/.php-cs-fixer.cache
/.rector.cache

# Per-developer tool settings. `.claude/launch.json` stays tracked — it defines how to run this
# project's dev server and is the same for everyone. `settings.local.json` is one machine's
# permission allowlist and has no business in a shared history.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Private keys and certificates, wherever they land. The repository should never be the reason a
# certificate leaks, and a developer who drops one in the project root should not have to
# remember this rule.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
!/storage/oauth-*.key.example
